From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 13:40:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 118/118] An Action records the root UI it was made over: no
 undo into a closed sound editor

ActionLogger::getNewAction() recorded getCurrentUI(). The sound editor's
note editor and note row editor may make Actions (they edit notes on the
grid), so such an Action recorded the sound editor. Undone from another
clip, revert() changes clip (CHANGE_CLIP) and made the recorded UI the root
UI: the sound editor, closed long before, opened with no menu item and
called through null in SoundEditor::beginScreen() (the fuzzer's seed 260,
stop run 11). Undo and redo run only from a root UI
(allowedToDoReversion()), and revert() compares the recorded view only with
root UIs, so the Action now records getRootUI().

Test (beta-1.3/tests/repro/undo_note_row_editor_emu.py): a note set in
PADA's note row editor, then from PADB's clip view BACK (undo): back in
PADA's clip view (before: a crash in SoundEditor::beginScreen()).
---
 src/deluge/model/action/action_logger.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/deluge/model/action/action_logger.cpp b/src/deluge/model/action/action_logger.cpp
index a34c1da2..5cdf9029 100644
--- a/src/deluge/model/action/action_logger.cpp
+++ b/src/deluge/model/action/action_logger.cpp
@@ -192,7 +192,10 @@ Action* ActionLogger::getNewAction(ActionType newActionType, ActionAddition addT
 		// newAction->modKnobModeSongView = currentSong->modKnobMode;
 		newAction->affectEntireSongView = currentSong->affectEntire;
 
-		newAction->view = getCurrentUI();
+		// The view to go back to on undo or redo: the root UI. An Action made in the sound editor (or another UI over a
+		// view) recorded that UI, and revert() then made the sound editor the root UI (CHANGE_CLIP), with no menu
+		// item to show: a call through null
+		newAction->view = getRootUI();
 		newAction->viewIsArrangerAutomation = (newAction->view == &automationView && automationView.onArrangerView);
 		newAction->currentClip = getCurrentClip();
 	}
